Qwen3.8-Flash-Next decode patch 07: cache host K/V rows in the staging arena.

vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py
vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py

With VLLM_QSA_KV_OFFLOAD=1 each decode step reads the rows its QSA indexer
selected, up to 2048 per layer (4 MiB), from host memory over PCIe. The read
cannot start before that layer's indexer has run, so it does not overlap with
other work: ~2 ms of a ~12 ms step once the context passes 2,048 tokens.
Consecutive steps select mostly the same rows.

The prefill staging arena (96 MiB per GPU) is idle between prefills. Decode
batches of up to 12 rows now keep the rows they read in it, one direct-mapped
region per QSA layer keyed by the physical cache slot, and read the hits from
there. A K/V write drops the row it replaces, and a staged prefill drops them
all. A hit reads the same bytes as the host copy, so the attention output is
bit-identical. Apart from ~0.4 MiB of tags per GPU it uses no memory.

On 3 x RTX 3090, 86-97% of the rows hit. Single-stream median inter-token
latency at 8k-160k context goes from 12.1-12.5 to 10.3-10.9 ms, and four
streams at 8k go from 16.8 to 14.9 ms.

Set VLLM_QSA_ROW_CACHE=0 to read every row from host memory again. It needs a
staging arena, so VLLM_QSA_KVO_ARENA=0 turns it off too.

